{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "The implementation language is Go, as indicated by the use of GoDoc and the Hyperledger Fabric context.",
    "API chaining (U3) will be implemented by creating intermediate wrapper types (e.g., Application, Org) that hold references to the underlying ConfigGroup proto and expose the appropriate getters and setters.",
    "SetXXX functions (U1) will replace existing values or append if not present for slices, ensuring no duplicates are added.",
    "Removal functions (U6) will return nil and not error if the value being removed does not exist.",
    "The new configtx CLI (U8) will be developed using a standard Go CLI framework (e.g., spf13/cobra) to handle commands and flags efficiently.",
    "Orderer and MSP types (U4, U5) will be moved to new subpackages without moving the associated functions unless strictly necessary for compilation."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The developer is highly experienced with Go and Hyperledger Fabric internals.",
    "Existing unit tests will need to be updated to reflect the new API signatures, package locations, and chained calls.",
    "1 workday equals 8 hours of development effort.",
    "The CLI will be a separate binary within the existing repository structure.",
    "No new external dependencies are required beyond standard Go libraries and existing Fabric dependencies."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Refactor Set/Update/Add and Removal Functions",
      "activity_description": "Rename AddXXX and UpdateXXX functions to SetXXX. Implement override behavior for existing values, handle slices carefully to avoid duplicates. Update removal functions to not return an error if the value does not exist. Update associated GoDocs.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "Rename Base/Updated Functions",
      "activity_description": "Rename Base() and Updated() functions to BaseConfig and UpdatedConfig (or similar appropriate names). Update associated GoDocs.",
      "most_likely_effort": 0.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "Implement API Chaining",
      "activity_description": "Extend subtypes with associated getters and setters to allow API chaining (e.g., c.Application().Org(orgName).AddAnchorPeer()). Create intermediate wrapper types as necessary. Update examples and GoDoc.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "Namespace Orderer Types",
      "activity_description": "Move orderer related types (Kafka, EtcdRaft, BatchSize, ConsensusState) to a separate orderer package within the configtx library. Ensure the new package is well documented.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "Namespace Membership Types",
      "activity_description": "Move msp related types (SigningIdentityInfo, OUIdentifier, CryptoConfig, NodeOUs) to a separate membership package within the configtx library. Ensure the new package is well documented.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "Refactor GoDocs and Examples",
      "activity_description": "Improve documentation around configtx.New(). Remove unnecessary examples. Rename Example_XXX functions to be more appropriate. Split up examples into more distinct ones. Remove output validation from examples. Fix horizontal scrolling in code blocks.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "Develop Configtx CLI",
      "activity_description": "Create a demo/sample configtx CLI that utilizes the configtx package. Implement commands and flags for generating system channel genesis blocks, application create channel transactions, and config updates. Add help/manual documentation.",
      "most_likely_effort": 5.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "Testing and Integration",
      "activity_description": "Update existing unit tests to match new API signatures and package locations. Add new tests for chained API calls and the new CLI. Ensure all changes compile and pass continuous integration.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3.0
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 20.5
  }
}
```

